# Accepted Trivy findings, one CVE/GHSA ID per line.
# Every entry needs a reason and an owner, and should be revisited each sprint.
# Example:
# CVE-2025-00000  # not reachable: we never call the affected API (owner: <name>, review: <date>)

# spring-webmvc 6.2.19 (Spring Boot 3.5.16, the latest 3.5.x). The flaw is in XsltView,
# which we never use (no XSLT views in the app). The only open-source fix is Spring 7.0.9
# (Spring Boot 4), a major upgrade to plan separately. (owner: NathanCarr10, review: 2026-10-20)
CVE-2026-47884

# Same spring-webmvc 6.2.19 and the same Spring 7.0.9-only fix as above. The flaw is in
# Server-Sent Events rendered through views. The only SSE endpoint, the support chat's
# /api/v1/support/conversations/{id}/events (SupportService.subscribe), sends a plain
# string and JSON message objects, never a view or ModelAndView. (owner: NathanCarr10,
# review: 2026-10-21)
CVE-2026-47890

# pillow 12.3.0, pulled in by Streamlit for the dashboard. The flaw is in Pillow's JPEG
# decoder; the fix is only in Pillow 13.0.0, which no Streamlit release accepts yet
# (1.65.0 and 1.66.0 both require pillow<13). The dashboard decodes no images from users:
# no st.image, file_uploader or camera_input, and its only image is our own favicon.
# Upgrade once Streamlit allows pillow 13. (owner: NathanCarr10, review: 2026-10-23)
CVE-2026-112403
